      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T22:58:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like fork() is already covered: since aosp/4368093, the branch just below gives a forked mm the parent\u0027s page size from the start, and `arch_dup_mmap()` sets it again with `mm_dup_mmap()` (aosp/4312467).\n\nAs far as I can see, `dup_mm()` is the only path that gets here with a non-zero `pte_shift`, and it always takes that branch (`@p` is the child and `current-\u003emm` is the mm being copied), while `mm_alloc()` zeroes the mm for `execve()`. With this check, I think that branch would become unreachable.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this hunk?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "8475aaf56ddacf20bdb7ff8bbbacd6d7d9f194db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
