      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T22:58:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that `do_mmap()` passes `__get_unmapped_area()` the offset in process pages (`arch/arm64/kernel/sys.c` shifts it by the per-process `PAGE_SHIFT`), so this keeps `mremap()` consistent with `mmap()`.\n\nWould you mind moving the conversion into a helper next to `vma_file_offset_at()` in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h`, so that `vrm_set_new_addr()` keeps a one-line change? Something like:\n\n```\n    pgoff_t pgoff \u003d vma_mmap_pgoff(vma, vrm-\u003eaddr);\n```\n\nI think `vma-\u003evm_file` alone would do for the file check, since `__get_unmapped_area()` zeroes `pgoff` when there is no file.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "8475aaf56ddacf20bdb7ff8bbbacd6d7d9f194db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
