      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T22:58:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the line this replaces already keeps the source slice: since aosp/4312522, an `mremap()` destination in a 4KB process is always at the same slice of its 16KB window as the source (`mm_mremap_fixed_keeps_slice()` rejects other `MREMAP_FIXED` targets, and `mm_mremap_get_unmapped_area()` picks one at that slice for the rest). So `vma_slice_offset(vma, addr)` gives the same slice as `vma_slice_offset(vma, old_addr)`.\n\nThe merge path relies on the same thing: `VMG_VMA_STATE()` fills `vmg.slice_off` from the destination address as well (aosp/4366900).\n\nWould it be OK to keep `copy_vma()` and the `vma_set_slice_off()` line as they are? Then `old_addr` wouldn\u0027t be needed in `copy_vma()`, `mm/vma.h` and `mm/mremap.c`, and neither would the new `copy_vma_slice_off()` and `copy_vma_set_range()` helpers.",
      "isAi": true,
